		"context": "WARDEN on the security office PA. The Watcher moves only when unseen; GET /cameras shows live camera states; the guard's name on the sign-in sheet is smudged (LIKE 'Har%'); a door command reports success but the door has an actuator fault (the first terminal lie)."},
	{"id": "l2_voicemail", "level": 2, "title": "Vale's voicemail", "wired": true,
		"moment": "Leaving a message on a desk answering machine, late at night.",
		"context": "The answering machine on the night desk blinks: one message, stamped SUN 10/12 1:52 AM. That is before her last badge swipe and before the memo was scanned, so it must not hint that she is alive (the reveal is at the end of Level 10). Optional, near the desk."},
	{"id": "l2_huddles", "level": 2, "title": "Book huddles: LIKE and GET", "wired": false,
		"moment": "At the workbench with your crew while they read a beginner's book together. One line to start each chapter, one to wrap it up.",
		"context": "Garage flashback huddles for the LIKE and GET chapters."},
	{"id": "l2_crew", "level": 2, "title": "Crew commentary: security floor", "wired": false,
		"moment": "Thinking out loud while the crew works through a security floor at night: badge logs, a door on a timer, cameras, a smudged sign-in sheet, a stubborn door and a keypad.",
		"context": "Commentary for the security floor puzzles (badge_log, lab_door, cameras, pike, door, har)."},
	{"id": "l4_huddles", "level": 4, "title": "Book huddles: UPDATE and INSERT", "wired": true,
		"moment": "At the workbench with your crew while they read a beginner's book together. One line to start each chapter, one to wrap it up.",
		"context": "Garage flashback huddles for the UPDATE chapter ('Never forget the WHERE', the lesson the main_doors accident teaches) and the INSERT chapter (Adding a row)."},
	{"id": "l4_epsilon", "level": 4, "title": "Containment protocol Epsilon", "wired": true,
		"moment": "Over every speaker in the building: the building's computer announces a full lockdown. Then, every few minutes, a reminder.",
		"context": "Act 2: the crew opens main_doors thinking it's the front entrance; it's the entity containment doors. WARDEN (cold phase) seals the building. The terminal's lie at the main entrance is exposed by the crew's own SELECT, not by WARDEN. Level 4 under curriculum option B (approved 2026-10-21)."},
	{"id": "l4_writes_suspended", "level": 4, "title": "Writes suspended", "wired": true,
		"moment": "Over every speaker in the building, just after someone has changed something at a terminal: the building's computer makes one more announcement.",
		"context": "Ground floor, after the crew's main-entrance UPDATE says '1 row affected' and the latch clicks: Epsilon reverts the write and WARDEN announces that the database is now read-only, which is why the crew turns to the building's services. Placement chosen by Augustine 2026-10-21 ('After the lie')."},
	{"id": "l4_read_only", "level": 4, "title": "Writes refused", "wired": true,
		"moment": "Someone types a change into a terminal during the lockdown. The building's computer answers over the speakers and on the screen.",
		"context": "After the read-only announcement, any change the crew types is refused; SELECT still works. By Level 4 WARDEN's fault lets his own personality leak out: the first refusal is the automatic PA announcement first, then WARDEN himself, teasing, as a separate beat. Approved by Augustine 2026-10-21 with that split."},
	{"id": "l4_floor_10", "level": 4, "title": "Floor 10: Plant and Power", "wired": true,
		"moment": "A mechanical floor full of breakers and door controllers. The building's computer watches you work, over the ceiling speakers, between its own cheerful pre-recorded announcements.",
		"context": "WARDEN becomes version 3.0 here. Before the main_doors accident he still waits politely for a PA tape to finish and says THIS UNIT. The accident is his first big failure: he revises his protocols and says I in an announcement for the first time (l4_upgrade_2). After it he talks over the PA tapes. Mixed lines are the automatic announcement first, then his own voice as a separate beat. The floor 22 I and my lines stay as the fault's first slips. Approved by Augustine 2026-10-21."},
	{"id": "l4_lobby", "level": 4, "title": "The lobby, locked in", "wired": true,
		"moment": "Back on the ground floor, the building locked tight. As you give up on the front doors and head for the stairs, the building's computer has a reminder for you.",
		"context": "After the main-entrance lie and the read-only announcement, when the crew heads for the stairs up to floor 9. Lift service is already suspended. Approved by Augustine 2026-10-21."},
	{"id": "l5_huddles", "level": 5, "title": "Book huddles: Acceptable API's", "wired": false,
		"moment": "Your crew finds a beginner's book on a desk and reads it together on the spot. One line to start each chapter, one to wrap it up.",
		"context": "Found in the payroll office on floor 9, the same series as Easy SQL. The crew reads aloud themselves (no Maddison in the tower). The title, Acceptable API's, is Augustine's. Lines approved by Augustine 2026-10-21."},
	{"id": "l6_huddles", "level": 6, "title": "Book huddles: Easy JavaScript", "wired": false,
		"moment": "Your crew finds another beginner's book, under a coffee mug, and reads it together on the spot. One line to start each chapter, one to wrap it up.",
		"context": "Found on B1 next to where the deck's script editor arrives. Variables and loops are used on Level 6; functions, lists and testing on Level 7. Title is a placeholder until Augustine names it. Approved by Augustine 2026-10-21."},
	{"id": "l8_huddles", "level": 8, "title": "Book huddles: Hello HTML!", "wired": false,
		"moment": "In a lift, your crew finds another beginner's book tucked behind the handrail and reads it together on the ride. One line to start each chapter, one to wrap it up.",
		"context": "Found in the elevator after Level 7. Elements and attributes are used on Level 8, the CSS chapters on Level 9, forms on Level 10. 'Who keeps leaving these?' answers nothing. The title is Augustine's. Lines approved by Augustine 2026-10-21."},
]

## speaker, text (also the subtitle), and a short note for the actor.
const LINES := {
	# --- Level 0 -------------------------------------------------------------
	"l0_brief_1": {"scene": "l0_garage", "speaker": "MADDISON", "text": "Okay! Everybody comfy? Look at you. My whole company, in one garage.",
		"note": "Big, warm, delighted to have an audience. The crew is already sitting, facing her."},
	"l0_brief_1_solo": {"scene": "l0_garage", "speaker": "MADDISON", "text": "Okay! Look at you. My whole company, in one seat.",
		"note": "Solo version. The same joke, a little teasing."},
	"l0_brief_2": {"scene": "l0_garage", "speaker": "MADDISON", "text": "Where we stand. Rent's due Friday, the van's held together with tape, and our best client is a library that pays in exact change.",
		"note": "Cheerful, as if it's good news. Counting it off on her fingers."},
	"l0_brief_3": {"scene": "l0_garage", "speaker": "MADDISON", "text": "So this year's goal was simple. Stay open. Maybe a second van. Maybe a sign that doesn't fall off.",
		"note": "Every 'maybe' a little grander, then the sign brings it back down to earth."},
	"l0_brief_4": {"scene": "l0_garage", "speaker": "MADDISON", "text": "Forget all that. We got Halcyon. The overnight database contract. Ours.",
		"note": "Building to it. She can't stand still for 'Ours.'"},
	"l0_brief_5": {"scene": "l0_garage", "speaker": "MADDISON", "text": "How? I underbid everybody. By a lot. Don't ask how much. Job's tonight, eleven o'clock.",
		"note": "Quickly, before anyone can ask."},
	"l0_bag": {"scene": "l0_garage", "speaker": "MADDISON", "text": "You guys are too excited! Go hit the punching bag to blow off some steam. When you're done, come sit down.",
		"note": "Laughing, shooing them off."},
	"l0_bag_solo": {"scene": "l0_garage", "speaker": "MADDISON", "text": "You're too excited! Go hit the punching bag to blow off some steam. When you're done, come sit down.",
		"note": "Solo version. Laughing, shooing them off."},
	"l0_bag_back": {"scene": "l0_garage", "speaker": "MADDISON", "text": "Better? Good. Now eyes on me, gorgeous people.",
		"note": "Once everyone's back in their seats. A little flirty, played light, like a coach."},
	"l0_bag_back_solo": {"scene": "l0_garage", "speaker": "MADDISON", "text": "Better? Good. Now eyes on me, gorgeous.",
		"note": "Solo version. A little flirty, played light, like a coach."},
	"l0_workorder": {"scene": "l0_garage", "speaker": "MADDISON", "text": "I put a copy of the work order in each of your notebooks. Pull it out and take a look.",
		"note": "Pleased with herself for being organized."},
	"l0_workorder_solo": {"scene": "l0_garage", "speaker": "MADDISON", "text": "I put a copy of the work order in your notebook. Pull it out and take a look.",
		"note": "Solo version. Pleased with herself for being organized."},
	"l0_book_catch": {"scene": "l0_garage", "speaker": "MADDISON", "text": "Small problem. It says database. And unless one of you secretly knows SQL...",
		"note": "The smile stays on. She leaves the sentence hanging and waits. Nobody does."},
	"l0_book_catch_solo": {"scene": "l0_garage", "speaker": "MADDISON", "text": "Small problem. It says database. And unless you secretly know SQL...",
		"note": "Solo version. The smile stays on. She leaves the sentence hanging and waits."},
	"l0_bookstore": {"scene": "l0_garage", "speaker": "MADDISON", "text": "...I stopped by the bookstore. Easy SQL. 'Learn databases in a weekend.' We've got till eleven.",
		"note": "Proud of this. Holding up the receipt, not the book."},
	"l0_grab": {"scene": "l0_garage", "speaker": "MADDISON", "text": "It's in the shop bag on the shelf by the side door. One of you go grab it.",
		"note": "Pointing at the side door to the house."},
	"l0_grab_solo": {"scene": "l0_garage", "speaker": "MADDISON", "text": "It's in the shop bag on the shelf by the side door. Go on, grab it for me.",
		"note": "Solo version. Pointing at the side door to the house."},
	"l0_whiteboard": {"scene": "l0_garage", "speaker": "MADDISON", "text": "Thank you! Okay. Whiteboard. Chapter zero. We're reading this together.",
		"note": "When whoever got the book sits down. Uncapping a marker with a flourish, like she's about to teach a class she's never taken.",
		"jot": "Read chapter zero of Easy SQL together before we go"},
	"l0_whiteboard_solo": {"scene": "l0_garage", "speaker": "MADDISON", "text": "Thank you! Okay. Whiteboard. Chapter zero. Let's read this together.",
		"note": "Solo version. Uncapping a marker with a flourish.",
		"jot": "Read chapter zero of Easy SQL together before we go"},
	"l0_garage_5": {"scene": "l0_garage", "speaker": "MADDISON", "text": "Look at that. You're practically engineers. Take the book with you. Everybody in the van.",
		"note": "Genuinely thrilled. After the huddle's quiz."},
	"l0_garage_5_solo": {"scene": "l0_garage", "speaker": "MADDISON", "text": "Look at that. You're practically an engineer. Take the book with you. Into the van.",
		"note": "Solo version. Genuinely thrilled. After the huddle's quiz."},
	"l0_garage_6": {"scene": "l0_garage", "speaker": "MADDISON", "text": "Rules for tonight. Nod a lot. Anything you don't know, you need to check the logs. And if anyone asks, we've got a fleet. You're van three. I'll be on the radio.",
		"note": "At the van door, counting the rules off. She stays behind.",
		"jot": "Maddison's rule: anything we don't know, check the logs."},
	"l0_huddle_select_1": {"scene": "l0_huddles", "speaker": "MADDISON", "text": "Chapter one. SELECT, FROM, and a semicolon. That's it? That's a whole language?",
		"note": "Disbelieving, delighted."},
	"l0_huddle_select_2": {"scene": "l0_huddles", "speaker": "MADDISON", "text": "Book says never forget the semicolon. Says it twice. So I'm saying it twice. Semicolon.",
		"note": "Deadly serious about the one thing they're sure of."},
	"l0_huddle_order_1": {"scene": "l0_huddles", "speaker": "MADDISON", "text": "Chapter two. 'Putting things in order.' Now that, I can get behind.",
		"note": "Reading off the page."},
	"l0_huddle_order_2": {"scene": "l0_huddles", "speaker": "MADDISON", "text": "Smallest first, unless you say DESC. Write that down. I'm writing it down.",
		"note": "Scribbling."},
	"l0_dispatch_1": {"scene": "l0_van", "speaker": "MADDISON", "text": "Van three, you're on site at Halcyon Data Systems. After-hours callout.",
		"note": "Over the van radio, in the professional dispatcher voice. 'Van three' is a bluff: they own one van."},
	"l0_dispatch_2": {"scene": "l0_van", "speaker": "MADDISON", "text": "They've got a database problem. Contact is Dale Rourke, facilities. He'll meet you at the front doors.",
		"note": "Reading it off the ticket."},
	"l0_dispatch_3": {"scene": "l0_van", "speaker": "MADDISON", "text": "Work order's in your notebook, the usual: diagnose, tidy up whatever tables they point you at, get a sign-off. Hop out when you're ready. Dispatch out.",
		"note": "Bored, reading the form. Signing off, already onto the next call."},
	"l0_greet_1": {"scene": "l0_arrive", "speaker": "ROURKE", "text": "There you are. Dale Rourke, facilities. I'll be your escort tonight.",
		"note": "Waiting outside the front doors as the crew walks up. Friendly, a handshake in the voice."},
	"l0_greet_3": {"scene": "l0_arrive", "speaker": "ROURKE", "text": "Badge rules after hours. You don't go anywhere I don't take you.",
		"note": "Still smiling. Should sound like a joke the first time and a threat on replay.",
		"jot": "After hours we don't go anywhere Rourke doesn't take us."},
	"l0_greet_4": {"scene": "l0_arrive", "speaker": "ROURKE", "text": "Come on in. I'll sign you in at the front desk.",
		"note": "Holding the door, waving them through."},
	"l0_pa_1": {"scene": "l0_arrive", "speaker": "PA", "text": "Good evening! Halcyon Data Systems is now closed.",
		"note": "Over the lobby PA, as the crew steps inside. Pleasant, like a store closing announcement."},
	"l0_pa_2": {"scene": "l0_arrive", "speaker": "PA", "text": "Visitors must remain with their escort at all times. Thank you for your cooperation!",
		"note": "Same announcement, continuing."},
	"l0_greet_2": {"scene": "l0_arrive", "speaker": "ROURKE", "text": "Sorry about that. The company loves its PA system.",
		"note": "Inside the lobby, right after the PA. Chuckling, waving at the ceiling speaker."},
	"l0_signin": {"scene": "l0_arrive", "speaker": "ROURKE", "text": "Doors lock themselves after hours. Don't worry, I've got the badge. Sign the visitor log for me.",
		"note": "Casual, reassuring. Nothing to worry about. (On a replay it lands differently.)"},
	"l0_badges": {"scene": "l0_arrive", "speaker": "ROURKE", "text": "Visitor badges. Keep them on you. Doors upstairs won't let you through without one.",
		"note": "Handing them over the desk, routine. Helpful, a little bored.",
		"jot": "Keep the visitor badges on. Doors upstairs need them."},
	"l0_tour_1": {"scene": "l0_tour", "speaker": "ROURKE", "text": "Here's the job. Dr. Vale, our lead engineer, went missing three nights ago.",
		"note": "Walking. Matter-of-fact, the way you'd mention the weather."},
	"l0_tour_2": {"scene": "l0_tour", "speaker": "ROURKE", "text": "Her systems are a mess and the director wants them recovered by morning. Quietly.",
		"note": "Small beat before \"Quietly.\"",
		"jot": "Dr. Vale, the lead engineer, has been missing three nights. The director wants her systems recovered by morning."},
	"l0_tour_3": {"scene": "l0_hall", "speaker": "ROURKE", "text": "Fun fact, while we walk: the man who founded this place, Harold Mercer, hated computers running buildings.",
		"note": "Tour-guide mode, enjoying himself."},
	"l0_tour_4": {"scene": "l0_hall", "speaker": "ROURKE", "text": "Board fired him when they installed WARDEN. That's the AI that runs the campus now.",
		"note": "Still chatting to the crew, a little proud of the trivia."},
	"l0_tour_5": {"scene": "l0_hall", "speaker": "ROURKE", "text": "Old-timers say Mercer built himself a safe room somewhere in here. Off the grid. Unhackable.",
		"note": "Spooky-campfire voice, playing it up.",
		"secret": true},
	"l0_tour_6": {"scene": "l0_hall", "speaker": "ROURKE", "text": "Ghost stories. Anyway.",
		"note": "Dropping it fast. He doesn't want them thinking about it."},
	"l0_desk_1": {"scene": "l0_tour", "speaker": "ROURKE", "text": "The front desk scanner ate one of Vale's memos. The scraps went into a table.",
		"note": "Pointing at the desk.",
		"jot": "Rourke: the front desk scanner \"ate\" one of Vale's memos. The scanner's card might say where it went.", "case": "memo", "found_in": ["ScanRight 3000 - Quick Start"]},
	"l0_desk_2": {"scene": "l0_tour", "speaker": "ROURKE", "text": "Director wants to know what it said. Go ahead, terminal's on the desk.",
		"note": "Casual, but he wants to know too."},
	"l0_sort_hint": {"scene": "l0_memo", "speaker": "PA", "text": "Employees are reminded to shred all documents in the marked company shredders! Your files belong to Halcyon!",
		"note": "From the ceiling speakers. A canned reminder that plays every hour. Proud of the company, unaware of anyone listening."},
	"l0_memo_flag": {"scene": "l0_memo", "speaker": "ROURKE", "text": "Nice work. I'll make sure that goes straight to the director.",
		"note": "Pleased, jotting it on his clipboard before he's read it. Warm; on a replay it's the worst thing he says all night."},
	"l0_memo_1": {"scene": "l0_memo", "speaker": "ROURKE", "text": "...Huh. She always was dramatic.",
		"note": "A beat too long before he speaks. Covering."},
	"l0_caller_1": {"scene": "l0_memo", "speaker": "ROURKE", "text": "One thing on your paperwork. It says I called you in. I didn't. That call came from building services.",
		"note": "Mild, a little puzzled, tapping the work order. Not suspicious yet."},
	"l0_caller_2": {"scene": "l0_memo", "speaker": "ROURKE", "text": "Want to know who? The staff directory's on that terminal.",
		"note": "Helpful, easygoing. Nodding at the terminal.",
		"jot": "Rourke says he didn't call us in. So who did?", "case": "caller"},
	"l0_mailroom_1": {"scene": "l0_memo", "speaker": "ROURKE", "text": "Mailroom. Clerk's got the only phone list in this building that's actually up to date. She pinned it to the wall so nobody walks off with it.",
		"note": "Nodding down the back corridor toward the mailroom. Amused, a little fond.",
		"jot": "Rourke: the only phone list that's up to date is the one pinned up in the mailroom.", "case": "caller", "found_in": ["HALCYON STAFF DIRECTORY"]},
	"l0_mailroom_2": {"scene": "l0_floor", "speaker": "ROURKE", "text": "Don't touch the outgoing tray. Last guy who did got a memo about it.",
		"note": "Only if a player goes inside the mailroom. Mock-serious."},
	"l0_caller_3": {"scene": "l0_memo", "speaker": "ROURKE", "text": "Mercer? Huh. That line's been dead for years. Somebody's having fun with the phones. Anyway.",
		"note": "A beat of real surprise, then he brushes it off and moves on."},
	"l0_memo_2": {"scene": "l0_memo", "speaker": "ROURKE", "text": "Grab the walkie-talkies from lost and found, back behind the desk.",
		"note": "Back to friendly, changing the subject."},
	"l0_memo_3": {"scene": "l0_memo", "speaker": "ROURKE", "text": "And yes, you hop the counter. Company's big on fitness, so there's no gate. Means nobody sneaks back there either.",
		"note": "Amused, he's said this to every visitor. A little eye-roll at corporate."},
	"l0_memo_4": {"scene": "l0_memo", "speaker": "ROURKE", "text": "Grab one and I'll take you to the server room.",
